## 3. Data Model Changes

| Column    | Type      | Nullable | Default         |
|-----------|-----------|----------|-----------------|
| id        | {id type} | No       | {generated how} |
| {field}   | {type}    | No       | —               |`,
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    heading: 'Test Cases',
    templatePath: 'templates/TC-Test-Cases.md',
    artefactsPath: 'artefacts/test-cases/{MODULE}/',
    description: 'One file per test case, grouped by module under test-cases/. Test plans come from a different producer — the /generate-test-plan power skill — so they live in test-plans/{MODULE}/, joined to their cases by the module name. Baxter never generates happy path tests alone — every set must cover all four types and always includes data validation and label accuracy scenarios. Once a suite is saved, Baxter mentions that a Test Plan (TP) can follow via /generate-test-plan — a TC suite is a prerequisite for a TP, never the reverse, and Baxter never runs it automatically.',
    templates: [
      {
        name: 'TC — Test Case',
        path: 'templates/TC-Test-Cases.md',
        sections: ['Metadata (ID, priority, type, linked PRD + PD, FR/AC)', 'Preconditions', 'Step / Action / Input / Expected Result table', 'Postconditions', 'Execution log'],
        preview: `# Test Case: {MODULE}_TC{NN}_{Short_Name}

> **Status:** DRAFT | READY | PASS | FAIL | BLOCKED
> **Priority:** High / Medium / Low
> **Type:** Happy Path / Negative / Role-Based / Edge Case
